  "_comment": "Keyed by GitHub Linguist canonical language name so the output of `github-linguist --json` joins directly. `aliases` lists alternate names that have been observed in older Linguist or in enry. Verified against PMD 7.24.0 JAR contents: every `default_ruleset` path was confirmed shipped in the relevant `pmd-<lang>.jar`. Java and Apex use their bundled `rulesets/<lang>/quickstart.xml`; other languages use a `bestpractices + errorprone` pair as the most actionable default for learning, except Visualforce (security only) and XSL (codestyle only), which have narrower coverage upstream. PMD also parses many other languages for CPD (copy-paste detection) only — C/C++, C#, CSS, Dart, Fortran, Gherkin, Go, Groovy, Julia, Lua, Matlab, Objective-C, Perl, PHP, Python, Ruby, Rust, T-SQL, Coco. These ship no rule-based rulesets and are therefore not actionable by this plugin.",
